{"chunk_id": "aa8d07213081", "text": "Rama sits with the sage while Bharata, accompanied by ministers and citizens, approaches him in humility. The gathered assembly senses that a decisive appeal is coming. Bharata, grieving over their father\u2019s death and ashamed of Kaikeyi\u2019s actions, begs Rama to return to Ayodhya and assume the throne that rightfully belongs to him. Declaring himself Rama\u2019s servant despite being Kaikeyi\u2019s son, he pleads for Rama to relieve the kingdom\u2019s sorrow. Bharata even places his head at Rama\u2019s feet in anguish. Rama responds with compassion but firm resolve: a son must obey his father\u2019s command. Since their father ordered his exile, Rama insists he must remain in the forest for fourteen years and urges Bharata to rule instead.\nBharata begs Rama to return and rule Ayodhya, but Rama refuses, insisting on obeying their father's command to live in exile for fourteen years.\nThemes: filial duty, renunciation of power, brotherly devotion, obedience to dharma", "vector": [0.015141808427870274, -0.021634956821799278, -0.029884448274970055, 0.002689400687813759, -0.020424144342541695, 0.013758022338151932, -0.010564670898020267, 0.003025367856025696, -0.03211979568004608, -0.001343037118203938, 0.019093580543994904, -0.01001914031803608, -0.005222460255026817, 0.01387777365744114, -0.018787551671266556, -0.010997104458510876, 0.04289735481142998, -0.01256051566451788, 0.03419547155499458, 0.005771317519247532, 0.006712690927088261, -0.010198766365647316, -0.004557178821414709, 0.012287750840187073, -0.01854805089533329, 0.00208732089959085, 0.015594200231134892, -0.032625406980514526, 0.01991852931678295, -0.02103620395064354, -0.00586113054305315, -0.016605427488684654, 0.007710613310337067, -0.0057779704220592976, -0.01777632348239422, 0.015381310135126114, -0.010651158168911934, 0.003256553318351507, 0.01539461500942707, -0.0014320185873657465, 0.013252409175038338, -0.015940146520733833, -0.01502205803990364, -0.